+++ b/README.md
@@ -199,6 +199,7 @@ Temporary development diagnostic: `-wex-adlp-readout` captures ADL-P boot resour
 Temporary development diagnostic: `-wex-reset-trace` records each GPU hang recovery step (channel restart, engine reset, scheduler reset and resume, command-streamer reset) with the render engine's reset and ring registers in the `WEXGPUResetTrace` registry property. It does not change recovery.
 Experimental: `-wex-reset-restore` saves the render engine's mode, status-page, chicken and user-mode whitelist registers and its cache-control (MOCS and L3) tables just before a render-domain GPU hang reset and writes them back after the reset, before work is replayed, on GPUs where the reset clears them, and completes stamps whose work the reset lost: two seconds after the reset, and later whenever a waiter times out on one that has stopped moving. It also enables the reset trace.
 Experimental: `-wex-no-multicontext` disables the donor's second (multi-context compute) command streamer, so compute work runs on the render engine.
+Experimental: `-wex-pm` applies the XE-PM CPU profile for hybrid Alder Lake / Raptor Lake under XCPM 20 s after boot: it rescales XCPM's HWP request to the P-cores' real highest performance (XCPM's 100 MHz units cap them about 20% low), sets EPP 0, turns off energy-efficient turbo, enables C8/C10 and disables the non-existent C3 in XCPM's idle table, and puts driverless IPU/GNA/ISH/DPTF/Thunderbolt DMA functions in D3hot. Status is in `WEXPowerProfile` and `sysctl debug.xepm`.
 Experimental: `-wex-scanout-coherent` treats every surface the donor flips to a display plane as displayable, so its later rendering uses the donor's display-safe (not LLC-cached) MOCS. The display engine does not snoop the LLC; without this, a downscaled HiDPI backing larger than the panel shows unflushed, partly drawn frames.
 `-wex-adlp-load-only` blocks both native framebuffer and accelerator probes/starts on a selected ADL-P/RPL-P device, for load-only diagnostics without GPU initialization.
 `-wex-display13-offline` keeps native display controller initialization enabled on Alder Lake-N / Twin Lake and Alder Lake-H/P/U / Raptor Lake-H/P/U but reports selected outputs as disconnected, isolating HPD/EDID and mode programming for framebuffer diagnostics. It does not establish display operation.
